{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant plus a motion-capability plant, then encode the exploration policy in compact deterministic specifications. The policy makes random_walk the default in clear space, inserts a short forward pulse for progress, uses one-shot obstacle recovery states with directed turns, and reserves full_rotate for a last-resort blocked-front case. Uncontrollable events are total in every specification state, with path_clear usually self-looping in action/recovery states so intended one-shot controllable pulses are not preempted unless a safety-critical obstacle event occurs.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and actuation into plant automata and place the exploration logic in specifications",
    "Use exactly one controllable action in each explore/recovery state, with random_walk in the initial clear state and directed one-shot recovery after obstacle events",
    "Bias toward coverage by returning quickly from recovery to clear exploration and by alternating random_walk with short move_forward progress",
    "Keep obstacle-left and obstacle-right responses consistent with single preferred turn directions and avoid enabling both turn directions in the same state",
    "Use full_rotate only in a dedicated front-blocked last-resort recovery state"
  ],
